  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "As the Natal dan Tahun Baru (Nataru) holiday season approaches, the Indonesian government is implementing comprehensive measures to manage public safety and supply chain logistics. The Coordinating Ministry for Political and Security Affairs confirmed that the police will oversee the period with over 77,000 personnel. Simultaneously, the Ministry of Trade is monitoring basic commodity prices, noting that while costs remain relatively stable, beef prices have faced upward pressure due to international supplier dynamics. Additional efforts include market surveillance by regional food task forces and the establishment of toll road communication channels. Infrastructure entities like PLN are coordinating with legal authorities to ensure electricity reliability, while logistics and transportation preparations remain a priority to accommodate increased holiday traffic. Officials have urged traders to maintain fair pricing practices as the country prepares for the influx of travelers and heightened consumer demand during the upcoming festive season.",
